    description: DOI of version 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/JehanneDussert/underlaid"
url: "https://underlaid.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  For 2,752 IRIS neighborhoods across Paris, Hauts-de-Seine,
  Seine-Saint-Denis and Val-de-Marne, counts how many of four categories
  (thermal, air/noise pollution, housing, access to care) are
  simultaneously in their metro-wide worst quartile (a score from 0 to 4,
  since version 0.2.0; 0 to 3 in version 0.1.0), and sets that count
  beside residents' means to cope (median income, overcrowding, secondary
  residences), measured on a separate axis. Access to care counts GPs and
  pharmacies reachable on foot and by public transport, shared among
  everyone who can reach them (E2SFCA); inclusive mobility (step-free
  travel) is published for information. Built entirely from French public
  open data; methodology documented in SCORING.md. Code under MIT; the
  published data files are under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
keywords:
